Hi Marc et al.,

Similarly, the Zipkin lab at MSU developed this  <https://danaus.shinyapps.io/Danaus/>shiny app (https://danaus.shinyapps.io/Danaus/) to (hypothetically) demonstrate how varying environmental/habitat factors could impact the monarch butterfly population size in the future. It uses exactly what you mention - a slider bar - to set desired values for each management scenario, and the code is provided on the right-hand side of the interface. We developed it for an outreach event for Girls Math and Science Day (6th - 8th graders) to get young women excited about coding and ecology!

Hope this helps - and feel free to email the main developer, Alex Wright (adwr...@msu.edu), with any questions.

Best,
